Package: haishoku
Title: Colour Palettes from Sanzo Wada's 'A Dictionary of Color Combinations'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Barrett", "Wolfe", , "barrett.wolfe@utas.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Matt", "DesLauriers", role = "cph",
           comment = "Transcribed colour data (MIT licence)"),
    person("Dain M.", "Blodorn Kim", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Original transcription of the colour data")
  )
Description: The 159 colours and 348 two-, three- and four-colour combinations
    in Sanzo Wada's 'A Dictionary of Color Combinations' (Seigensha, 2010),
    a re-edition of his 'Haishoku Soukan' (1933-34). Each colour keeps its name and the
    book's CMYK printing recipe alongside sRGB and CIELAB values, and every
    colour can be looked up in the combinations it appears in. Palettes work in
    base graphics and as discrete, continuous and binned 'ggplot2' scales, with
    helpers to rank combinations by perceptual distinctness and colour vision
    deficiency safety, extend a combination with further dictionary colours,
    find the nearest dictionary colour to any colour, assign information-design
    roles, and export palettes for other tools.
